so P is Z0, w1 is Z1.

01:31:03.530 --> 01:31:04.660 align:middle line:90%
Right?

01:31:04.660 --> 01:31:07.105 align:middle line:90%
YAEL KALAI: Yes.

01:31:07.105 --> 01:31:07.605 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

01:31:07.605 --> 01:31:12.736 align:middle line:90%


01:31:12.736 --> 01:31:13.670 align:middle line:90%
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

01:31:13.670 --> 01:31:14.337 align:middle line:90%
YAEL KALAI: Yes.

01:31:14.337 --> 01:31:14.940 align:middle line:90%
Yes, yes, yes.

01:31:14.940 --> 01:31:16.190 align:middle line:90%
Through the name you're right.

01:31:16.190 --> 01:31:16.750 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

01:31:16.750 --> 01:31:19.330 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

01:31:19.330 --> 01:31:20.190 align:middle line:90%
Z0, yes.

01:31:20.190 --> 01:31:21.000 align:middle line:90%
Yes, you're right.

01:31:21.000 --> 01:31:21.710 align:middle line:90%
You're right.

01:31:21.710 --> 01:31:25.500 align:middle line:84%
You're right, and this is still
a low-degree polynomial in Z0.

01:31:25.500 --> 01:31:26.220 align:middle line:90%
Good point.

01:31:26.220 --> 01:31:30.230 align:middle line:84%
It's sitting-- yeah, maybe
I erased it, but this.

01:31:30.230 --> 01:31:32.220 align:middle line:90%
No, but I didn't write this.

01:31:32.220 --> 01:31:34.247 align:middle line:84%
STUDENT: We need it
though below the--

01:31:34.247 --> 01:31:35.205 align:middle line:90%
YAEL KALAI: Below here?

01:31:35.205 --> 01:31:37.730 align:middle line:90%


01:31:37.730 --> 01:31:40.880 align:middle line:90%
No, but I need to write--

01:31:40.880 --> 01:31:48.173 align:middle line:90%
it's like this is xi minus--

01:31:48.173 --> 01:32:00.130 align:middle line:90%


01:32:00.130 --> 01:32:00.680 align:middle line:90%
I think.

01:32:00.680 --> 01:32:01.240 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

01:32:01.240 --> 01:32:06.700 align:middle line:84%
So it's-- oh, maybe I need
to take extension of this.

01:32:06.700 --> 01:32:07.660 align:middle line:90%
Sorry, one second.

01:32:07.660 --> 01:32:11.700 align:middle line:90%
This is-- hold on.

01:32:11.700 --> 01:32:12.340 align:middle line:90%
Sorry.

01:32:12.340 --> 01:32:13.320 align:middle line:90%
Maybe I missed this.

01:32:13.320 --> 01:32:15.970 align:middle line:84%
Let me think because
I missed in the notes.

01:32:15.970 --> 01:32:16.690 align:middle line:90%
So hold on.

01:32:16.690 --> 01:32:31.360 align:middle line:84%
So here the point is H. I think
I need to take extension of this

01:32:31.360 --> 01:32:39.720 align:middle line:84%
too, because the point here,
this is not a polynomial in H.

01:32:39.720 --> 01:32:41.510 align:middle line:90%
OK, so let's do that carefully.

01:32:41.510 --> 01:32:42.670 align:middle line:90%
Sorry, I missed that.

01:32:42.670 --> 01:32:46.590 align:middle line:84%
So chi is a
low-degree polynomial,

01:32:46.590 --> 01:32:49.340 align:middle line:84%
but it's a low-degree
polynomial in x.

01:32:49.340 --> 01:32:52.850 align:middle line:84%
It's not a low-degree
polynomial in this H. H here

01:32:52.850 --> 01:32:57.800 align:middle line:84%
is in the denominator, so it's
not a low-degree polynomial

01:32:57.800 --> 01:33:00.585 align:middle line:90%
