01:33:00.585 --> 01:33:03.200 align:middle line:90%


01:33:03.200 --> 01:33:05.840 align:middle line:90%
But you can extend, so it's OK.

01:33:05.840 --> 01:33:06.550 align:middle line:90%
Don't worry.

01:33:06.550 --> 01:33:08.050 align:middle line:84%
So it's not a
low-degree polynomial.

01:33:08.050 --> 01:33:09.930 align:middle line:90%
However, it is in--

01:33:09.930 --> 01:33:24.270 align:middle line:84%
all we care about is, if we
think of it as a function of Z0

01:33:24.270 --> 01:33:27.120 align:middle line:90%
of p, then we just extend.

01:33:27.120 --> 01:33:36.410 align:middle line:84%
We can-- I just
want to make sure

01:33:36.410 --> 01:33:38.660 align:middle line:84%
