01:34:44.990 --> 01:34:47.650 align:middle line:90%
But there is, actually.

01:34:47.650 --> 01:34:50.050 align:middle line:84%
The low-degree polynomial
is one of them.

01:34:50.050 --> 01:34:52.810 align:middle line:90%
So the answer is yes, there is.

01:34:52.810 --> 01:34:56.300 align:middle line:90%
It's the low-degree-- yeah.

01:34:56.300 --> 01:34:58.930 align:middle line:84%
So it's defined
only on H. You can

01:34:58.930 --> 01:35:01.450 align:middle line:90%
think of it as defined only--

01:35:01.450 --> 01:35:03.740 align:middle line:90%
this chi is an extension.

01:35:03.740 --> 01:35:06.310 align:middle line:84%
This chi on its
own is extension.

01:35:06.310 --> 01:35:07.490 align:middle line:90%
What is this chi?

01:35:07.490 --> 01:35:09.890 align:middle line:90%
This chi is a function.

01:35:09.890 --> 01:35:12.760 align:middle line:90%
You can think-- OK, sorry.

01:35:12.760 --> 01:35:14.710 align:middle line:90%
