01:35:47.080 --> 01:35:49.156 align:middle line:90%
Chi is the extension--

01:35:49.156 --> 01:35:51.790 align:middle line:90%


01:35:51.790 --> 01:35:53.335 align:middle line:90%
OK, let me rewrite this.

01:35:53.335 --> 01:35:57.520 align:middle line:90%


01:35:57.520 --> 01:36:10.680 align:middle line:84%
Chi H1 up to Hm,
Z1 up to Zm is just

01:36:10.680 --> 01:36:14.880 align:middle line:90%
multiplication of chi Hi, Zi.

01:36:14.880 --> 01:36:16.420 align:middle line:90%
So it's exactly the same thing.

01:36:16.420 --> 01:36:19.390 align:middle line:84%
I just don't want to put Hi on
the bottom, like I did before.

01:36:19.390 --> 01:36:21.070 align:middle line:90%
So let me put it as a variable.

01:36:21.070 --> 01:36:22.450 align:middle line:90%
I didn't change anything.

01:36:22.450 --> 01:36:25.240 align:middle line:84%
And now this original--
what is this?

01:36:25.240 --> 01:36:28.870 align:middle line:84%
This is the low-degree
extension of the function.

01:36:28.870 --> 01:36:32.260 align:middle line:84%
Let me first define
chi and H to the 2m.

01:36:32.260 --> 01:36:35.220 align:middle line:84%
So chi is such that
an H to the 2m,

01:36:35.220 --> 01:36:43.530 align:middle line:84%
so for every Hi or for
every H and Z in H to the m,

01:36:43.530 --> 01:36:50.460 align:middle line:84%
chi HZ is equal to 1 if and
only if H is equal to Z.

01:36:50.460 --> 01:36:53.370 align:middle line:84%
I only define an H to
the m, now extended.

01:36:53.370 --> 01:36:57.340 align:middle line:84%
That's how we define chi, the
unique low-degree extension.

01:36:57.340 --> 01:36:58.870 align:middle line:90%
What is exactly the extension?

01:36:58.870 --> 01:37:01.100 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, it's this multiplication,
blah, blah, blah.

01:37:01.100 --> 01:37:03.790 align:middle line:90%
I don't want to go into it.

01:37:03.790 --> 01:37:05.560 align:middle line:84%
But it's just a
unique extension.

01:37:05.560 --> 01:37:09.210 align:middle line:90%


01:37:09.210 --> 01:37:11.030 align:middle line:90%
So now with that--

01:37:11.030 --> 01:37:14.320 align:middle line:90%


01:37:14.320 --> 01:37:17.920 align:middle line:84%
and the reason
there is a unique--

01:37:17.920 --> 01:37:22.710 align:middle line:84%
actually, I should say,
this is kind of chi 1.

01:37:22.710 --> 01:37:25.320 align:middle line:90%


01:37:25.320 --> 01:37:27.670 align:middle line:84%
And the reason there
is a unique extension--

01:37:27.670 --> 01:37:29.541 align:middle line:90%
this is kind of H1, Hi, Zi.

01:37:29.541 --> 01:37:32.510 align:middle line:90%


01:37:32.510 --> 01:37:34.260 align:middle line:84%
And the reason there
is a unique exception

01:37:34.260 --> 01:37:37.440 align:middle line:84%
is from the Lagrange
interpolation theorem.

01:37:37.440 --> 01:37:41.100 align:middle line:84%
So it's just a multiplication
of the unique kind of Lagrange

01:37:41.100 --> 01:37:42.590 align:middle line:90%
interpolation extensions.

01:37:42.590 --> 01:37:44.800 align:middle line:84%
So all I did here--
so sorry about this,

01:37:44.800 --> 01:37:48.240 align:middle line:84%
but all I did here is I
changed the notation from the H

01:37:48.240 --> 01:37:50.590 align:middle line:84%
kind of as a subscript
to H as input.

01:37:50.590 --> 01:37:53.830 align:middle line:84%
And now I'm treating
them both symmetrically,

01:37:53.830 --> 01:37:55.480 align:middle line:84%
which was important
because otherwise.

01:37:55.480 --> 01:37:56.560 align:middle line:90%
So thank you.

01:37:56.560 --> 01:37:57.725 align:middle line:90%
Wow, you guys are great.

01:37:57.725 --> 01:38:00.940 align:middle line:90%


01:38:00.940 --> 01:38:04.650 align:middle line:84%
So now let's fix
the mistake here.

01:38:04.650 --> 01:38:11.510 align:middle line:90%
So this is chi of P and Zi.

01:38:11.510 --> 01:38:14.940 align:middle line:90%


01:38:14.940 --> 01:38:17.080 align:middle line:84%
We're summing over P,
but Zi is an input.

01:38:17.080 --> 01:38:18.630 align:middle line:84%
That's the input
we started with.

01:38:18.630 --> 01:38:20.130 align:middle line:90%
That's the claim.

01:38:20.130 --> 01:38:21.660 align:middle line:90%
Good.

01:38:21.660 --> 01:38:25.990 align:middle line:84%
But for me, chi is a
