01:38:41.580 --> 01:38:43.692 align:middle line:90%
YAEL KALAI: Why?

01:38:43.692 --> 01:38:45.150 align:middle line:84%
STUDENT: So the
definition for chi,

01:38:45.150 --> 01:38:46.908 align:middle line:84%
doesn't it only appear
in the denominator?

01:38:46.908 --> 01:38:49.200 align:middle line:84%
YAEL KALAI: OK, so let's look
at the definition of chi.

01:38:49.200 --> 01:38:51.960 align:middle line:84%
The definition of
chi and m variables

01:38:51.960 --> 01:38:55.140 align:middle line:84%
is just-- so chi
takes two variables.

01:38:55.140 --> 01:38:58.360 align:middle line:84%
The definition of 2m variables,
just the multiplication,

01:38:58.360 --> 01:39:02.970 align:middle line:84%
i goes from 1 to m of
a chi 1 on Hi and Zi.

01:39:02.970 --> 01:39:06.710 align:middle line:84%
So now I need to
define what is chi 1.

01:39:06.710 --> 01:39:09.530 align:middle line:84%
Oh, you're saying
