01:39:09.530 --> 01:39:11.650 align:middle line:84%
You're saying it's
not one variable.

01:39:11.650 --> 01:39:14.830 align:middle line:84%
STUDENT: Or rather
more like in chi 1,

01:39:14.830 --> 01:39:18.360 align:middle line:90%
isn't it not a polynomial in Hi?

01:39:18.360 --> 01:39:19.610 align:middle line:90%
YAEL KALAI: It's a polynomial?

01:39:19.610 --> 01:39:24.530 align:middle line:84%
No, I only think of it as
a polynomial in Hi and Zi.

01:39:24.530 --> 01:39:25.877 align:middle line:90%
Chi-- sorry.

01:39:25.877 --> 01:39:27.710 align:middle line:84%
OK, maybe I didn't
understand your question.

01:39:27.710 --> 01:39:30.850 align:middle line:84%
Chi 1 is a two-variate
polynomial.

01:39:30.850 --> 01:39:31.760 align:middle line:90%
It has two variables.

01:39:31.760 --> 01:39:32.427 align:middle line:90%
So you're right.

01:39:32.427 --> 01:39:36.280 align:middle line:84%
It's two variables,
not one, because I

01:39:36.280 --> 01:39:37.540 align:middle line:90%
said it reduces to Lagrange.

01:39:37.540 --> 01:39:38.998 align:middle line:84%
You're saying, no,
Lagrange is one.

01:39:38.998 --> 01:39:41.050 align:middle line:90%
I'm thinking it is 2.

01:39:41.050 --> 01:39:42.290 align:middle line:90%
That's what you said, right?

01:39:42.290 --> 01:39:43.150 align:middle line:90%
Or maybe I didn't--

01:39:43.150 --> 01:39:44.650 align:middle line:84%
STUDENT: I guess
my question is more

01:39:44.650 --> 01:39:48.080 align:middle line:84%
